Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to implement per-key stateful streaming logic, rolling window calculations, and safe downstream signaling with offset semantics. It also probes handling of out-of-order arrivals and ensuring at-least-once delivery by committing only after alert emission succeeds.

Key Concepts
- Per-key state management
- Rolling window calculations (60s)
- Threshold-based anomaly detection
- Idempotent downstream writes and offset commits
- Canary test design for spike vs. normal data

Code Example
